# Build output
bin/
obj/
artifacts/
*.user
.vs/
*_debug.log
native/ddraw_inproc/build/*.obj

# --- Never publish -------------------------------------------------------------
# Every pattern below is anchored with a leading slash so it matches the repository
# root and nothing else. An unanchored `runtime/` also matches src/Login38.Aux/Runtime/,
# which silently drops twenty source files and leaves a clone that cannot build — git on
# Windows folds case, so the capital R is no protection. Anchor these.

# An operator's generated package. pack.properties holds the RSA private exponent;
# list.txt and config.ini are that server's encrypted settings, and the fixed cipher key
# is a constant in this repository, so publishing them publishes the server. A player
# gets these from their own server, never from here.
/dist/
/pack.properties
/list.txt
/config.ini
/launcher.ini

# The same files copied in as test fixtures. The tests that read them skip when they are
# absent — see tests/Shared/ShippingPackageFact.cs.
tests/*/TestData/list.txt
tests/*/TestData/config.ini

# Game data and shipping layouts carried in for manual testing. Not source.
/runtime/
/data/SPR.txt

# Working notes from the port. Local research log, not documentation.
/findings.md
/progress.md
/task_plan.md
/bot_plan.md

# Raw memory captured while reverse engineering. Reproducible from a running client with
# the scripts in tools/, and megabytes of it, so it is kept out.
/_effectlist.raw
*.raw

# The original Rust implementation, kept locally as the behavioural specification.
/rust-reference/

# Local UI-automation helper with machine-specific paths.
/.drive.ps1
